<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<!--
╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║                       UPCOMING EVENTS TILE v1.1                            ║
║              Multi-Calendar Agenda Display for SharpTools                  ║
║                  with Home Assistant iCal Integration                      ║
╠════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣
║                                                                            ║
║  VERSION 1.1 CHANGELOG:                                                    ║
║  • ADDED: Three-language localization (English, Portuguese, Spanish)       ║
║  • ADDED: Normalized date format "Ddd, Mmm DD" identical across locales    ║
║  • ADDED: Localized relative-time hint (In X days / Em X dias / En X dias) ║
║  • ADDED: Two-line description with ellipsis overflow                      ║
║  • IMPROVED: Language selected via dropdown instead of free text           ║
║  • REMOVED: Static tile header (the native SharpTools label is used)       ║
║                                                                            ║
║  DESCRIPTION:                                                              ║
║  A unified "what's coming up" tile that merges up to four calendars into   ║
║  a single chronological agenda. It combines national holidays, inter-      ║
║  national observances, and personal travel itineraries (TripIt) into one   ║
║  list - something the native SharpTools calendar tile cannot do, being     ║
║  limited to a fixed 7-day window and a single calendar. The merge, sort,   ║
║  and trim logic runs in a Home Assistant backend; this tile focuses on     ║
║  presentation and stays resilient to feed changes.                         ║
║                                                                            ║
║  KEY FEATURES:                                                             ║
║  • Up to four merged calendars in one chronological list                   ║
║  • Per-row flag/icon (UN flag, country flag, travel, custom)               ║
║  • Source label, localized date, relative-time hint, description           ║
║  • Three-language output (en-US, pt-BR, es-ES)                             ║
║  • Configurable number of events to display                               ║
║  • Two-line description clamp with ellipsis                                ║
║  • "Today" emphasis with accent color                                      ║
║  • Optional gradient background                                            ║
║  • Automatic responsive scaling for all screen sizes                       ║
║  • Single unified codebase - ZERO DUPLICATION                              ║
║                                                                            ║
║  TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE:                                                   ║
║  • Unified Codebase: one implementation for phone, tablet, and desktop     ║
║  • Zero CSS Duplication: shared rules declared once; media queries only    ║
║    override the few dimensions that scale (font sizes, widths, paddings)   ║
║  • Dynamic Responsive Fit: auto-adapts at <=480px and >=768px breakpoints  ║
║  • Reuse over Repetition (DRY): emoji, date, and relative-hint helpers      ║
║    are implemented once and reused per row                                 ║
║  • Component-Based, Modular Organization for maintainability               ║
║  • Read-Only External Interaction: subscribes to a single Thing attribute  ║
║    and never issues device commands                                        ║
║  • Classic (ES5-style) JavaScript for broad device compatibility           ║
║                                                                            ║
║  MODULE ORGANIZATION (logical use order):                                  ║
║  Configuration -> State -> DOM References -> Internationalization ->        ║
║  Emoji Resolution -> Parsing -> Date Formatting -> Rendering ->             ║
║  Subscription -> Application Controller                                     ║
║                                                                            ║
║  INPUT DATA CONTRACT (Thing attribute string):                            ║
║  Records separated by " ~ " and fields by "|":                            ║
║    source|type|code|isoDate|title ~ source|type|code|isoDate|title ~ ...   ║
║  • source : free text shown in the source column (e.g. Panama, TripIt)     ║
║  • type   : un | country | trip | custom  (selects the leading emoji)      ║
║  • code   : country -> ISO-3166 alpha-2 (pa, us, it...); custom -> emoji;   ║
║             otherwise empty                                                 ║
║  • isoDate: YYYY-MM-DD (all-day) - used for display and ordering           ║
║  • title  : event description (the only field allowed to contain spaces)   ║
║                                                                            ║
║  Example Attribute Content:                                               ║
║  "Panama|country|pa|2026-11-03|Separation Day ~ TripIt|trip||2026-07-04|   ║
║   Check-in: The Buenaventura ~ Internacional|un||2026-10-31|Halloween"     ║
║                                                                            ║
║  CONFIGURATION OPTIONS (tile settings):                                   ║
║  • Calendar Thing ....... Thing exposing the events attribute (required)   ║
║  • Attribute name ....... attribute holding the string (default "payload") ║
║  • Number of events ..... rows to display; 0 = all available               ║
║  • Language / Idioma .... pt-BR | en-US | es-ES                            ║
║  • Show weekday ......... include the weekday in the date column           ║
║  • Use gradient ......... enable a gradient background                     ║
║  • Gradient base color .. base color used for the gradient                 ║
║                                                                            ║
║  FAILURE / DEGRADED OPERATION:                                            ║
║  • Missing Calendar Thing ......... shows a configuration message          ║
║  • Attribute not found ............ shows a configuration message          ║
║  • Empty / null value ............. shows a localized "no events" message  ║
║  • Malformed record (<5 fields) ... that record is skipped silently        ║
║  • Unparsable date ................ raw ISO text is shown as-is            ║
║  • Country flags on Windows ....... regional-indicator emoji may render    ║
║    as two letters (platform limitation); all other icons are unaffected    ║
║                                                                            ║
║  BACKEND NOTE:                                                            ║
║  A Home Assistant template sensor reads several iCal sensors, merges and   ║
║  sorts events by date, trims to a maximum, and writes the delimited        ║
║  string into a custom attribute (default "payload"). The sensor state is   ║
║  derived from the event count plus the current date so that any change     ║
║  forces a push update to SharpTools.                                       ║
║                                                                            ║
║  AUTHOR: Wilson Marcolin                                                   ║
║  CONTRIBUTORS: Claude AI Assistant                                         ║
║  VERSION: 1.1.0 - Multi-Language & Two-Line Descriptions                   ║
║  RELEASE: June 2026                                                        ║
║  LICENSE: MIT                                                              ║
║                                                                            ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
-->
  <script type="application/json" id="tile-settings">
    {
      "schema": "0.2.0",
      "name": "Upcoming Events v1.1",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "THING",
          "name": "eventsThing",
          "label": "Calendar Thing (with events attribute)",
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "type": "STRING",
          "name": "attrName",
          "label": "Attribute name holding the string",
          "default": "payload",
          "placeholder": "payload"
        },
        {
          "type": "NUMBER",
          "name": "maxShow",
          "label": "Number of events to display (0 = all)",
          "default": 6
        },
        {
          "type": "ENUM",
          "name": "locale",
          "label": "Language / Idioma",
          "default": "pt-BR",
          "values": [
            {"label": "Português (pt-BR)", "value": "pt-BR"},
            {"label": "English (en-US)", "value": "en-US"},
            {"label": "Español (es-ES)", "value": "es-ES"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "BOOLEAN",
          "name": "showWeekday",
          "default": true,
          "label": "Show weekday in date"
        },
        {
          "type": "BOOLEAN",
          "name": "useGradient",
          "default": false,
          "label": "Use Gradient Background"
        },
        {
          "type": "STRING",
          "name": "gradientColor",
          "label": "Gradient Base Color",
          "default": "#3f51b5",
          "placeholder": "#3f51b5"
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <script src="https://cdn.sharptools.io/js/custom-tiles/0.2.1/stio.js"></script>

  <style>
    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html, body {
      height: 100%;
      width: 100%;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: transparent;
    }

    /* Root container */
    .main-container {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: 32px 6px 6px 6px;   /* top space reserved for the SharpTools label */
      background: transparent;
      gap: 6px;
    }
    .main-container.gradient {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--grad-start) 0%, var(--grad-end) 100%);
    }

    /* Main content wrapper: must own the available height so the inner
       list can scroll. min-height:0 lets the flex child shrink and
       activate overflow instead of pushing content out of view. */
    #mainContent {
      flex: 1;
      min-height: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    /* Scrollable event list */
    .events-list {
      flex: 1;
      overflow-y: auto;
      overflow-x: hidden;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
      padding-right: 2px;
    }

    /* Single event row */
    .event-row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      background: #fff;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 6px 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
      border-left: 3px solid #3f51b5;
    }
    .gradient .event-row {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
      backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
      border-left-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);
    }

    /* Column 1: flag / icon */
    .ev-flag {
      font-size: 22px;
      line-height: 1;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      width: 26px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    /* Column 2: source label */
    .ev-origin {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      width: 78px;
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #3f51b5;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.2px;
      white-space: nowrap;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
    }
    .gradient .ev-origin { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); }

    /* Column 3: date + relative hint */
    .ev-date {
      flex-shrink: 0;
      width: 88px;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #1a237e;
      line-height: 1.15;
    }
    .gradient .ev-date { color: #fff; }
    .ev-date .rel {
      display: block;
      font-size: 8px;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #888;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .gradient .ev-date .rel { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); }

    /* Column 4: event description (clamped to two lines) */
    .ev-title {
      flex: 1;
      min-width: 0;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #333;
      line-height: 1.25;
      display: -webkit-box;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      word-break: break-word;
    }
    .gradient .ev-title { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95); }

    /* "Today" emphasis */
    .event-row.is-today { border-left-color: #ff9800; }
    .event-row.is-today .ev-date { color: #ff9800; }

    /* Loading / error / empty states */
    .loading-state, .error-state, .empty-state {
      width: 100%; height: 100%;
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;
    }
    .spinner {
      width: 36px; height: 36px;
      border: 4px solid #ddd; border-top-color: #3f51b5;
      border-radius: 50%; animation: spin 1s linear infinite;
    }
    @keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
    .msg { font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; padding: 0 16px; }
    .msg.err { color: #d32f2f; }
    .msg.info { color: #888; }
    .hidden { display: none !important; }

    /* Custom scrollbar */
    .events-list::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 3px; }
    .events-list::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: transparent; }
    .events-list::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
      background: rgba(0,0,0,0.2); border-radius: 2px;
    }

    /* Responsive overrides: small screens (phones) */
    @media (max-width: 480px) {
      .ev-origin { width: 60px; font-size: 9px; }
      .ev-date { width: 74px; font-size: 10px; }
      .ev-title { font-size: 11px; }
      .ev-flag { font-size: 19px; width: 22px; }
    }

    /* Responsive overrides: large screens (desktop) */
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
      .main-container { padding: 40px 10px 10px 10px; gap: 8px; }
      .ev-origin { width: 96px; font-size: 11px; }
      .ev-date { width: 104px; font-size: 13px; }
      .ev-title { font-size: 14px; }
      .ev-flag { font-size: 26px; width: 32px; }
      .event-row { padding: 8px 12px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div id="mainContainer" class="main-container">

    <div id="loadingState" class="loading-state">
      <div class="spinner"></div>
      <div style="font-weight:bold;color:#3f51b5;">Loading events...</div>
    </div>

    <div id="errorState" class="error-state hidden">
      <div class="msg err" id="errorMessage">Configuration Error</div>
    </div>

    <div id="mainContent" class="hidden">
      <div class="events-list" id="eventsList"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    (function () {
      'use strict';

      // ======================================================================
      //  Configuration Module
      //  User-facing options resolved from the tile settings at startup.
      // ======================================================================
      var Config = {
        maxShow: 6,
        locale: 'pt-BR',
        showWeekday: true,
        gradient: false,
        gradientColor: '#3f51b5'
      };

      // ======================================================================
      //  State Module
      //  Runtime data: the raw attribute string and the parsed event list.
      // ======================================================================
      var State = {
        raw: '',
        events: []
      };

      // ======================================================================
      //  DOM References Module
      //  Cached element handles, resolved once on startup.
      // ======================================================================
      var DOM = {};

      function initDOM() {
        var ids = [
          'mainContainer', 'loadingState', 'errorState',
          'mainContent', 'errorMessage', 'eventsList'
        ];
        for (var i = 0; i < ids.length; i++) {
          DOM[ids[i]] = document.getElementById(ids[i]);
        }
        return DOM.mainContainer !== null;
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Internationalization Module
      //  Language tables drive identical date and relative-hint formatting
      //  across locales, independent of the host browser locale.
      //  Weekday index 0 = Sunday; month index 0 = January.
      // ======================================================================
      var I18N = {
        'en-US': {
          wd: ['Sun', 'Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat'],
          mo: ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'],
          today: 'Today', tomorrow: 'Tomorrow', past: 'Past', empty: 'No upcoming events',
          inDays: function (n) { return 'In ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' day' : ' days'); },
          inWeeks: function (n) { return 'In ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' week' : ' weeks'); },
          inMonths: function (n) { return 'In ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' month' : ' months'); }
        },
        'pt-BR': {
          wd: ['Dom', 'Seg', 'Ter', 'Qua', 'Qui', 'Sex', 'Sáb'],
          mo: ['Jan', 'Fev', 'Mar', 'Abr', 'Mai', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Ago', 'Set', 'Out', 'Nov', 'Dez'],
          today: 'Hoje', tomorrow: 'Amanhã', past: 'Passado', empty: 'Nenhum evento próximo',
          inDays: function (n) { return 'Em ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' dia' : ' dias'); },
          inWeeks: function (n) { return 'Em ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' semana' : ' semanas'); },
          inMonths: function (n) { return 'Em ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' mês' : ' meses'); }
        },
        'es-ES': {
          wd: ['Dom', 'Lun', 'Mar', 'Mié', 'Jue', 'Vie', 'Sáb'],
          mo: ['Ene', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Abr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Ago', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dic'],
          today: 'Hoy', tomorrow: 'Mañana', past: 'Pasado', empty: 'No hay eventos próximos',
          inDays: function (n) { return 'En ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' día' : ' días'); },
          inWeeks: function (n) { return 'En ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' semana' : ' semanas'); },
          inMonths: function (n) { return 'En ' + n + (n === 1 ? ' mes' : ' meses'); }
        }
      };

      function lang() {
        return I18N[Config.locale] || I18N['en-US'];
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Emoji Resolution Module
      //  Maps a record's type/code to a single leading emoji.
      //   - un      : United Nations flag (international)
      //   - country : ISO-3166 alpha-2 -> regional-indicator flag
      //   - trip    : airplane (travel / TripIt)
      //   - custom  : code may carry an emoji directly
      // ======================================================================
      function flagFromISO(iso) {
        if (!iso || iso.length !== 2) return '🏳️';
        var base = 0x1F1E6;
        var cc = iso.toUpperCase();
        var a = base + (cc.charCodeAt(0) - 65);
        var b = base + (cc.charCodeAt(1) - 65);
        return String.fromCodePoint(a) + String.fromCodePoint(b);
      }

      function emojiFor(type, code) {
        switch ((type || '').toLowerCase()) {
          case 'un':      return '🇺🇳';
          case 'country': return flagFromISO(code);
          case 'trip':    return '✈️';
          case 'custom':  return code || '📌';
          default:        return '📅';
        }
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Parsing Module
      //  Splits the attribute string into structured event objects.
      //  Records: " ~ "   Fields: "|"   (title may itself contain "|")
      // ======================================================================
      function parseEvents(str) {
        var out = [];
        if (!str) return out;
        var records = str.split('~');
        for (var i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {
          var rec = records[i].trim();
          if (!rec) continue;
          var f = rec.split('|');
          if (f.length < 5) continue;
          out.push({
            origem: (f[0] || '').trim(),
            tipo: (f[1] || '').trim(),
            codigo: (f[2] || '').trim(),
            iso: (f[3] || '').trim(),
            titulo: f.slice(4).join('|').trim()
          });
        }
        return out;
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Date Formatting Module
      //  Produces a fixed "Ddd, Mmm DD" layout and a localized relative hint.
      //  All-day ISO dates are parsed as local dates to avoid timezone shift.
      // ======================================================================
      function parseISODate(iso) {
        var m = /^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})/.exec(iso);
        if (!m) return null;
        return new Date(parseInt(m[1], 10), parseInt(m[2], 10) - 1, parseInt(m[3], 10));
      }

      function startOfDay(d) {
        return new Date(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth(), d.getDate());
      }

      function relativeLabel(d) {
        var L = lang();
        var today = startOfDay(new Date());
        var diff = Math.round((startOfDay(d) - today) / 86400000);
        if (diff === 0) return L.today;
        if (diff === 1) return L.tomorrow;
        if (diff < 0) return L.past;
        if (diff < 7) return L.inDays(diff);
        if (diff < 30) return L.inWeeks(Math.round(diff / 7));
        return L.inMonths(Math.round(diff / 30));
      }

      function formatDate(d) {
        var L = lang();
        var wd = L.wd[d.getDay()];
        var mo = L.mo[d.getMonth()];
        var dd = ('0' + d.getDate()).slice(-2);
        if (Config.showWeekday) return wd + ', ' + mo + ' ' + dd;
        return mo + ' ' + dd;
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Rendering Module
      //  Builds the row markup from the parsed, optionally trimmed list.
      // ======================================================================
      function escapeHtml(s) {
        if (s == null) return '';
        return String(s)
          .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;')
          .replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
      }

      function render() {
        var list = DOM.eventsList;
        list.innerHTML = '';

        var evs = State.events.slice();
        if (Config.maxShow && Config.maxShow > 0) evs = evs.slice(0, Config.maxShow);

        if (!evs.length) {
          list.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state"><div class="msg info">' +
            escapeHtml(lang().empty) + '</div></div>';
          return;
        }

        var todayStart = startOfDay(new Date());

        for (var i = 0; i < evs.length; i++) {
          var e = evs[i];
          var d = parseISODate(e.iso);
          var row = document.createElement('div');
          row.className = 'event-row';
          if (d && startOfDay(d).getTime() === todayStart.getTime()) {
            row.className += ' is-today';
          }

          var dateMain = d ? formatDate(d) : e.iso;
          var dateRel = d ? relativeLabel(d) : '';

          row.innerHTML =
            '<div class="ev-flag">' + emojiFor(e.tipo, e.codigo) + '</div>' +
            '<div class="ev-origin">' + escapeHtml(e.origem) + '</div>' +
            '<div class="ev-date">' + escapeHtml(dateMain) +
              '<span class="rel">' + escapeHtml(dateRel) + '</span></div>' +
            '<div class="ev-title">' + escapeHtml(e.titulo) + '</div>';

          list.appendChild(row);
        }
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Subscription Module
      //  Binds to the Thing attribute, applies the initial value, and listens
      //  for updates. This is the only point of contact with external data.
      // ======================================================================
      function handleValue(value) {
        State.raw = value || '';
        State.events = parseEvents(State.raw);
        render();
      }

      function subscribeThing(thing, attrName) {
        if (!thing) return;
        attrName = attrName || 'payload';

        if (thing.subscribe) {
          thing.subscribe(attrName);
        }

        var attr = thing.attributes ? thing.attributes[attrName] : null;
        if (!attr) {
          showError('Attribute "' + attrName + '" not found on the selected Thing');
          return;
        }

        if (attr.value != null) handleValue(attr.value);
        return attr.onValue(function (v) { handleValue(v); });
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  View Helpers
      // ======================================================================
      function showView(name) {
        DOM.loadingState.classList.toggle('hidden', name !== 'loading');
        DOM.errorState.classList.toggle('hidden', name !== 'error');
        DOM.mainContent.classList.toggle('hidden', name !== 'main');
      }

      function showError(message) {
        DOM.errorMessage.textContent = message;
        showView('error');
      }

      function applyGradient() {
        if (!Config.gradient) return;
        var color = Config.gradientColor || '#3f51b5';
        DOM.mainContainer.classList.add('gradient');
        DOM.mainContainer.style.setProperty('--grad-start', color);
        DOM.mainContainer.style.setProperty('--grad-end', color + '66');
      }

      // ======================================================================
      //  Application Controller
      //  Startup sequence: resolve DOM, wait for stio, read settings, bind.
      // ======================================================================
      function init() {
        if (!initDOM()) return;
        if (typeof stio === 'undefined') {
          setTimeout(init, 200);
          return;
        }

        stio.ready(function (data) {
          var s = data.settings || {};

          Config.maxShow = parseInt(s.maxShow, 10);
          if (isNaN(Config.maxShow)) Config.maxShow = 6;
          Config.locale = s.locale || 'pt-BR';
          Config.showWeekday = s.showWeekday !== false;
          Config.gradient = s.useGradient === true;
          Config.gradientColor = s.gradientColor || '#3f51b5';

          if (!s.eventsThing) {
            showError('Please configure the Calendar Thing');
            return;
          }

          applyGradient();
          subscribeThing(s.eventsThing, s.attrName || 'payload');

          setTimeout(function () {
            render();
            showView('main');
          }, 800);
        });
      }

      // Bootstrap
      if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
      } else {
        init();
      }
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>